      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Nonalcoholics who, on a problem drinking inventory, responded \"yes\" to items reflecting a psychological dependence on alcohol, tended after alcohol ingestion to report a decrease in pain experienced in a cold pressor test. Conversely, those whose responses indicated no psychological dependence on alcohol tended to report pain increases after the consumption of alcohol."},
